Metadata-Version: 2.4
Name: todesanzeigen
Version: 0.1.0
Summary: OCR and structured extraction pipeline for Todesanzeigen images.
Requires-Python: >=3.11
Requires-Dist: google-cloud-documentai>=3.0.0
Requires-Dist: google-genai>=1.0.0
Requires-Dist: python-dotenv>=1.0.0

# Images labeled "clean" are images that seem to be of original electronic document form (not by taking a picture of the printed document) without contaminating information. Most of clean images contain standard printed fonts while some contain special fonts (like hand-written like fonts) and some include picture backgrounds, as opposed to standard white background.
# "Newspaper" images are ones that are camera/phone taken images of newspaper sections that typically are not angled/cropped perfectly and contain some unnecessary sections around the border that shouldn't be included for concern, with the main box of content centered. Some photos even include an "overview" picture that includes an entire newspapaer page with several boxes (these are just reference images), these shouldn't be processed as there are images that are taken of the individual boxes of the same page
# The content of these images, death announcement, is not necessarily the same in visual format/layout, as it's very flexible, but the main form is similar, so important information such as full name, birth+death date, cities, etc. are there with few outliers.  

